1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,672
Everyone you know has a number now.

2
00:00:03,692 --> 00:00:05,622
It's how many more times they'll forgive

3
00:00:05,642 --> 00:00:06,442
you.

4
00:00:06,732 --> 00:00:07,887
Your little brother.

5
00:00:07,907 --> 00:00:09,527
Three hundred and twelve.

6
00:00:09,547 --> 00:00:10,672
Your mum.

7
00:00:10,862 --> 00:00:12,396
Doesn't even have a number.

8
00:00:12,986 --> 00:00:14,667
Your best friend has one.

9
00:00:15,357 --> 00:00:16,415
Just one.

10
00:00:19,465 --> 00:00:21,470
It takes you one coffee to work out

11
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:22,252
the rule.

12
00:00:23,162 --> 00:00:23,717
Oh no.

13
00:00:23,737 --> 00:00:24,784
Sorry, sorry

14
00:00:24,804 --> 00:00:26,212
Ah, don't worry about it.

15
00:00:26,362 --> 00:00:27,112
Forty.

16
00:00:27,137 --> 00:00:28,331
Thirty-nine.

17
00:00:28,351 --> 00:00:30,112
Every time someone forgives you, it

18
00:00:30,132 --> 00:00:31,626
goes down by one.

19
00:00:32,617 --> 00:00:35,662
A toddler in the park has nine thousand.

20
00:00:35,682 --> 00:00:37,729
Toddlers forgive everyone.

21
00:00:37,749 --> 00:00:40,129
A man you have never met has four.

22
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:42,455
You decide not to find out why.

23
00:00:43,445 --> 00:00:44,975
Your boss has two.

24
00:00:44,995 --> 00:00:46,475
You have never been this early in your

25
00:00:46,495 --> 00:00:47,181
life.

26
00:00:47,201 --> 00:00:47,956
Morning.

27
00:00:47,976 --> 00:00:49,101
Is that a tie?

28
00:00:49,121 --> 00:00:50,574
It felt like a tie day.

29
00:00:50,594 --> 00:00:51,825
It's Sunday.

30
00:00:52,624 --> 00:00:54,149
Can I borrow your charger?

31
00:00:54,169 --> 00:00:55,134
And your jacket.

32
00:00:55,154 --> 00:00:56,101
And forty quid.

33
00:00:56,121 --> 00:00:57,874
You already have my charger.

34
00:00:57,894 --> 00:00:59,199
Then just the forty.

35
00:00:59,219 --> 00:01:01,276
Also, can I stay at yours for a bit?

36
00:01:01,426 --> 00:01:03,181
Three hundred and twelve.

37
00:01:03,201 --> 00:01:05,194
Little brothers are built for this.

38
00:01:06,104 --> 00:01:07,210
You never call.

39
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,407
I'm calling now.

40
00:01:08,427 --> 00:01:09,502
Then you're forgiven.

41
00:01:09,522 --> 00:01:10,496
Did you eat?

42
00:01:10,646 --> 00:01:12,976
The symbol over her head doesn't even

43
00:01:12,996 --> 00:01:13,713
flicker.

44
00:01:14,403 --> 00:01:15,867
And then there's Mira.

45
00:01:17,517 --> 00:01:19,872
Four hours away, at her new course.

46
00:01:19,892 --> 00:01:21,563
With a one over her head.

47
00:01:21,583 --> 00:01:23,688
One more mistake, and that's it.

48
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,402
Whatever "it" is.

49
00:01:25,422 --> 00:01:26,605
So you get careful.

50
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:27,930
You do the maths.

51
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:30,265
If every mistake costs one chance, the

52
00:01:30,285 --> 00:01:32,760
only safe amount of Mira is none.

53
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:35,080
Her call comes at nine.

54
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:36,550
You let it ring.

55
00:01:36,575 --> 00:01:38,380
A call is twenty minutes of things you

56
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,558
could say wrong.

57
00:01:39,578 --> 00:01:40,576
You alive?

58
00:01:40,726 --> 00:01:41,901
You write a reply.

59
00:01:41,921 --> 00:01:43,146
Then a shorter one.

60
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:44,356
Then a thumbs up.

61
00:01:45,346 --> 00:01:47,501
She sends a photo of her new flat.

62
00:01:47,521 --> 00:01:49,051
You don't say it's small.

63
00:01:49,071 --> 00:01:50,607
You don't say anything.

64
00:01:51,517 --> 00:01:53,399
Why are you being weird with Mira?

65
00:01:53,419 --> 00:01:54,745
I'm not being weird.

66
00:01:54,765 --> 00:01:55,470
She texted me.

67
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:55,745
Me.

68
00:01:55,765 --> 00:01:57,126
To ask if you're okay.

69
00:01:57,276 --> 00:01:59,106
Mira never texts Theo.

70
00:01:59,126 --> 00:02:01,162
Theo can't even spell okay.

71
00:02:01,182 --> 00:02:02,487
Showcase on Friday.

72
00:02:02,507 --> 00:02:03,477
My first one.

73
00:02:03,497 --> 00:02:04,323
Will you come?

74
00:02:04,473 --> 00:02:06,533
Four hours on a train.

75
00:02:06,553 --> 00:02:08,483
A whole evening of chances to get it

76
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:09,115
wrong.

77
00:02:09,135 --> 00:02:09,465
Can't.

78
00:02:09,485 --> 00:02:10,070
Work.

79
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:11,462
I'll watch the stream?

80
00:02:12,112 --> 00:02:13,256
You send it.

81
00:02:14,846 --> 00:02:17,001
Somewhere four hours away, she forgives

82
00:02:17,021 --> 00:02:17,611
you.

83
00:02:18,201 --> 00:02:19,128
Zero.

84
00:02:20,178 --> 00:02:22,207
You spent her last chance by doing nothing

85
00:02:22,227 --> 00:02:23,160
at all.

86
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:25,580
That night, you work out what you were

87
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,745
protecting.

88
00:02:26,765 --> 00:02:27,645
Not her.

89
00:02:27,665 --> 00:02:28,531
The number.

90
00:02:29,121 --> 00:02:31,844
And a zero has nothing left to protect.

91
00:02:32,834 --> 00:02:35,104
So on Friday, you get on the train.

92
00:02:35,124 --> 00:02:36,254
Four hours.

93
00:02:36,274 --> 00:02:38,109
For once, you don't rehearse a single

94
00:02:38,129 --> 00:02:38,998
sentence.

95
00:02:39,988 --> 00:02:40,713
You're late.

96
00:02:40,733 --> 00:02:42,088
You stand at the back.

97
00:02:42,108 --> 00:02:44,551
You clap too loud, at the wrong moment.

98
00:02:44,571 --> 00:02:45,641
That's my friend.

99
00:02:45,661 --> 00:02:46,513
He's weird.

100
00:02:47,563 --> 00:02:48,993
The audience laughs.

101
00:02:49,013 --> 00:02:50,188
She keeps going.

102
00:02:50,223 --> 00:02:51,223
She's good at this.

103
00:02:51,243 --> 00:02:52,529
You knew she would be.

104
00:02:54,039 --> 00:02:55,273
You said you couldn't come.

105
00:02:55,293 --> 00:02:56,258
I lied.

106
00:02:56,278 --> 00:02:57,875
I was scared of getting it wrong.

107
00:02:57,895 --> 00:02:59,325
So you just disappeared?

108
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:00,800
That's the only thing that actually

109
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:01,511
hurts.

110
00:03:02,011 --> 00:03:02,391
I know.

111
00:03:02,411 --> 00:03:03,564
I'm sorry.

112
00:03:04,514 --> 00:03:06,294
You wait for the number to go below

113
00:03:06,314 --> 00:03:07,066
zero.

114
00:03:07,676 --> 00:03:08,526
You're here now.

115
00:03:08,546 --> 00:03:10,166
Buy me chips, and we're even.

116
00:03:11,716 --> 00:03:12,466
Zero.

117
00:03:12,486 --> 00:03:13,699
Then, one.

118
00:03:13,719 --> 00:03:15,324
It turns out the number doesn't only

119
00:03:15,344 --> 00:03:16,312
go down.

120
00:03:17,302 --> 00:03:18,732
You buy the chips.

121
00:03:18,752 --> 00:03:20,807
You tell her the flat isn't small.

122
00:03:20,827 --> 00:03:22,732
You tell her it's very small, and very

123
00:03:22,752 --> 00:03:23,343
her.

124
00:03:23,363 --> 00:03:25,191
Okay, now you're being weird again.

125
00:03:25,211 --> 00:03:26,541
You said I was weird.

126
00:03:26,561 --> 00:03:27,626
On a stage.

127
00:03:27,646 --> 00:03:28,802
In front of everyone.

128
00:03:28,822 --> 00:03:30,645
I said you were my friend first.

129
00:03:31,295 --> 00:03:33,440
Over her head, the one glows, small

130
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:34,490
and gold.

131
00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:36,032
You stop looking at it.

132
00:03:38,422 --> 00:03:40,527
Would you want to know how many chances

133
00:03:40,547 --> 00:03:41,511
you have left?
